<idea-plugin>
    <id>com.jakubjirak.metalshader</id>
    <name>Metal Shader Support</name>
    <vendor email="support@jakubjirak.com" url="https://jakubjirak.com">Jakub Jirák</vendor>

    <description><![CDATA[
<h2>Metal Shader Support</h2>
<p>
  Build stunning GPU shaders with full IDE power. Metal Shader Support delivers comprehensive Metal Shading
  Language support — from intelligent code completion with 300+ documented keywords to real-time shader
  preview and GPU profiling.
</p>

<h2>Key Features</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>Metal 3.2 &amp; 4.0 Support</b> — Full syntax highlighting for the latest Metal specifications</li>
  <li><b>300+ Documented Keywords</b> — Context-aware completion with inline documentation</li>
  <li><b>Performance Analyzer</b> — Complexity scoring and optimization hints for shader code</li>
  <li><b>MPS Integration</b> — Metal Performance Shaders framework support</li>
  <li><b>10 Live Templates</b> — Boilerplate snippets for common shader patterns</li>
  <li><b>Code Folding &amp; Formatting</b> — Professional editing experience for Metal shaders</li>
</ul>

<h2>Why Metal Shader Support?</h2>
<p>
  Metal shader development deserves first-class IDE support. No more editing shaders in Xcode or plain
  text — get the same productivity features you expect for Swift and Objective-C.
</p>

<h2>Free vs Pro</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>Free:</b> Syntax highlighting, code completion, live templates, formatting</li>
  <li><b>Pro:</b> Live shader preview (60 FPS), Metal debugger panel, GPU profiler integration, cross-platform transpiler (Enterprise), and texture preview</li>
</ul>
]]></description>

